@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Integrating Artifacts with CI/CD";
    ViewData["ActiveMenu"] = "AzureDevOps";
}

<div class="container py-4">
    <p class="text-center lead">Integrating Azure Artifacts with CI/CD pipelines enhances software development by automating dependency management and ensuring consistent builds across environments.</p>
    <hr />

    <div class="mt-5">
        <h2>Why Integrate Artifacts with CI/CD?</h2>
        <p>Azure Artifacts integration with CI/CD enables teams to manage dependencies efficiently, automate builds, and deploy securely. Key benefits include:</p>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Automated Dependency Management:</strong> Ensures builds always use the correct package versions.</li>
            <li><strong>Consistent Builds:</strong> Avoids version mismatches across environments.</li>
            <li><strong>Improved Security:</strong> Prevents the use of unauthorized or vulnerable packages.</li>
            <li><strong>Faster Deployments:</strong> Reduces manual intervention and streamlines delivery.</li>
        </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="text-center mt-4">
        <img src="https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/devops/artifacts/media/ci-cd-artifacts.png" alt="CI/CD with Azure Artifacts" class="img-fluid rounded shadow-lg">
        <p class="text-muted mt-2"><small>CI/CD pipeline integration with Azure Artifacts</small></p>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-5">
        <h3>Setting Up CI/CD with Azure Artifacts</h3>
        <p>Follow these steps to integrate Azure Artifacts with an Azure DevOps pipeline.</p>
        <ol>
            <li><strong>Create an Azure Artifacts Feed:</strong> Navigate to Azure DevOps > Artifacts > Create a new feed.</li>
            <li><strong>Configure the Pipeline:</strong> Add tasks to restore and publish packages within Azure Pipelines.</li>
            <li><strong>Use Feeds in Builds:</strong> Reference the artifact feed in the pipeline YAML file.</li>
            <li><strong>Deploy the Application:</strong> Ensure package dependencies are correctly resolved before deployment.</li>
        </ol>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-5">
        <h3>Pipeline Configuration Examples</h3>
        <p>Below are YAML configurations for integrating NuGet, npm, and Maven packages into Azure Pipelines.</p>

        <h4>NuGet Integration</h4>
        <pre class="bg-light p-3 rounded">
trigger:
- main

pool:
  vmImage: 'windows-latest'

steps:
- task: NuGetCommand@2
  inputs:
    command: 'restore'
    feedsToUse: 'select'
    vstsFeed: 'MyAzureArtifactsFeed'
- script: dotnet build --configuration Release
        </pre>

        <h4>npm Integration</h4>
        <pre class="bg-light p-3 rounded">
steps:
- task: npmAuthenticate@0
  inputs:
    workingFile: ".npmrc"
- script: npm install
- script: npm run build
        </pre>

        <h4>Maven Integration</h4>
        <pre class="bg-light p-3 rounded">
steps:
- task: Maven@3
  inputs:
    mavenPomFile: 'pom.xml'
    goals: 'clean install'
    options: '-s settings.xml'
    publishJUnitResults: true
    testResultsFiles: '**/surefire-reports/TEST-*.xml'
        </pre>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-5">
        <h3>Best Practices for CI/CD Integration</h3>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Use Version Locking:</strong> Avoid unexpected package updates by specifying exact versions.</li>
            <li><strong>Enable Security Scans:</strong> Identify vulnerabilities in dependencies before deployment.</li>
            <li><strong>Automate Artifact Publishing:</strong> Push updated packages to feeds during the build process.</li>
            <li><strong>Implement Approval Gates:</strong> Require approvals before deploying to production environments.</li>
        </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-5">
        <p>By integrating Azure Artifacts with CI/CD pipelines, teams can streamline package management, enhance security, and improve deployment efficiency. Ensuring proper dependency resolution in automated builds contributes to a more stable and scalable development workflow.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="d-flex justify-content-start mt-4">
        <a href="@Url.Action("ManagePackages", "AzureDevOps")" class="btn btn-outline-secondary">&larr; Previous: Managing Packages</a>
    </div>
</div>
